# Line endings and binary files.
#
# Why this exists: the generators write LF, Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true want CRLF in
# the working tree, and a regeneration then marks files as modified whose content is
# byte-identical. The committed blobs are ALREADY LF, so this does not rewrite history or content
# for them -- it pins the WORKING TREE to LF as well, which is what removes the phantom
# modifications. Measured on 2026-10-07: one `resolve_schema.py --all` left 203 files listed as
# modified of which 127 were phantom, and a full regeneration left 135 listed with ZERO real
# content diff. In a repository several sessions share, that makes "whose change is this?"
# unanswerable by eye -- it cost a blocked rebase and several wrong readings of `git status` in a
# single day.
#
# Scope, measured with `git add --renormalize`: 238 files actually change, every one of them a
# build/**/_visited_properties.tsv whose blob is CRLF because it was committed from Windows. No
# _sources file, no tool, no schema, no .py or .yaml. The drift check compares _sources, whose
# blobs are already LF, so it cannot be affected -- and normalising those .tsv blobs makes them
# AGREE with what the Linux postprocess produces.

# Default: let git detect text, and keep LF in both the index and the worktree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The formats the tooling reads and writes, named explicitly so a generated file never depends on
# auto-detection.
*.json    text eol=lf
*.jsonld  text eol=lf
*.yaml    text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.ttl     text eol=lf
*.shacl   text eol=lf
*.py      text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.html    text eol=lf
*.jsx     text eol=lf
*.txt     text eol=lf

# Tabular text: diffable, so text -- but no filter should touch the cell contents, which carry
# superscripts and degree signs.
*.csv     text eol=lf
*.tsv     text eol=lf

# Binary. Explicit rather than auto-detected, because a workbook mangled by an eol filter is
# corrupt in a way nobody notices until they open it, and the 67 xlsx files here are the TAPP
# deliveries.
*.xlsx    binary
*.xlsm    binary
*.xltx    binary
*.docx    binary
*.pdf     binary
*.png     binary
*.jpg     binary
*.jpeg    binary
*.gif     binary
*.zip     binary
